                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1750-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Lewitt Audio LCT 440 Pure</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Lewitt LCT 440 PURE is a side-address condenser microphone aimed at all-around studio use. </p><p>It is descended from Lewitt&#8217;s other side-address studio condensers but is the so-called &#8220;distilled essence&#8221; of those microphones &#8212; hence the &#8220;PURE&#8221; moniker &#8212; meaning that it lack the pattern selection, clip indicators, pads, filters, and other features of its sibling mics.</p><p>It does, however, share some features with the other LCT mics, such as the body design and dual-layer head basket. Based on specifications and frequency response, we conclude that the capsule is the same K67-derived design used in Lewitt&#8217;s 640/640TS, 550, and 450 mics in the LCT line.</p><p>Like all Lewitt microphones, the LCT 440 PURE is designed in Austria and manufactured in Lewitt&#8217;s own factory in China.</p><p>The LCT 440 PURE ships with Lewitt&#8217;s proprietary shockmount, which allows the mic to be positioned with its face flush against a sound source (such as a guitar cabinet) if desired. The package also includes a microphone bag and magnetic pop screen. It is sold in a padded cardboard box.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Lewitt/LCT-440-Pure">Lewitt Audio LCT-440-Pure</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2017.</p>
